Here's a C function that returns the larger of two integers:

```c
int larger(int a, int b) {
    if (a > b) {
        return a;
    } else {
        return b;
    }
}
```

This function takes two integer arguments and returns the larger one. If the first argument is greater than the second, it returns the first argument. If the first argument is less than the second, it returns the second argument.

